# Server-Sent Events (SSE) Implementation Guide

## Backend SSE Implementation
Based on [server.js](mdc:backend/src/server.js) SSE endpoints:

### SSE Endpoint Setup
```javascript
app.get('/chat/:chatId/stream', (req, res) => {
    res.setHeader('Content-Type', 'text/event-stream');
    res.setHeader('Cache-Control', 'no-cache');
    res.setHeader('Connection', 'keep-alive');
    
    res.write(`data: ${JSON.stringify({ type: 'connected', chatId })}\n\n`);
    
    req.on('close', () => {
        console.log(`Client disconnected from chat ${chatId}`);
    });
});
```

### Streaming Response Pattern
```javascript
app.post('/chat/:chatId/sse', async (req, res) => {
    // Set SSE headers
    res.setHeader('Content-Type', 'text/event-stream');
    res.setHeader('Cache-Control', 'no-cache');
    res.setHeader('Connection', 'keep-alive');
    
    const onMessage = (message) => {
        res.write(`data: ${JSON.stringify({...message, chatId})}\n\n`);
    };
    
    await chatService.sendMessageSSE(prompt, onMessage);
    res.end();
});
```

## Frontend SSE Consumption
Based on [ChatBox.js](mdc:frontend/src/components/ChatBox.js):

### SSE Reader Pattern
```javascript
const response = await fetch(`/chat/${chatId}/sse`, {
    method: 'POST',
    headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },
    body: JSON.stringify({ prompt: userMessage })
});

const reader = response.body.getReader();
const decoder = new TextDecoder();

while (true) {
    const { done, value } = await reader.read();
    if (done) break;
    
    const chunk = decoder.decode(value);
    const lines = chunk.split('\n');
    
    lines.forEach(line => {
        if (line.startsWith('data: ')) {
            const data = JSON.parse(line.slice(6));
            // Handle streaming data
        }
    });
}
```

## Message Types
- `'connected'` - Initial connection confirmation
- `'ai'` - AI response chunks
- `'human'` - User messages
- `'system'` - System messages
- `'error'` - Error messages

## Error Handling
- Always handle connection drops gracefully
- Implement reconnection logic for production
- Log disconnections for monitoring
- Clean up resources on component unmount

## Performance Considerations
- Use streaming for long responses
- Implement message chunking for large payloads
- Handle backpressure in high-traffic scenarios
- Monitor connection limits and cleanup